Z||000000||ferrari_momo||10-21-2001||11:14 AM||||Hello my fiero friends,<BR>  If it weren't for Pennock's fiero forum and ebay, I would never get any traffic flow to my site.  now, I get many emails from people who came to my site (probably from ebay deal).  Lots of complints were made on the site.  please visit <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>  and tell me what do you think.  There is no key word search, example "fiero or 308 ".  Could it be because the site is too small?  I am sure that the webmaster would have told me everything i need to get the site going like all business should have.  <BR>  Some complints were: email address sounds unprofessional, no phone numbers, no shopping carts, pictures sometimes do not appear where it should be, website down, how would customer pay (paypal ,credit cards, etc) and so on.  Your inputs will help greatly.  I will not be offended if you tell me the truth.  I have had more than 50 emails on this topic.  and I lost sales because those people thing the fibersmith is another fake.  Only you guys know me here.  Thank you for your time reading this.  Every response counts.  Have a great day.<BR>sincerely yours,<BR>pat kalsmith <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||10-21-2001||11:47 AM||||The wheel page looks pretty shady- no brand name, no price, no nothing. Otherwise, its not bad at all, not too cluttered, but then again, not all too informative.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||Screwie||10-21-2001||12:47 PM||||The site is definitely too small. The Eurobodykit link was dead when I tried it. It doesn't come across to me as a real business. Maybe you should give detailed contact information, rather than a @yahoo address (make it @thefibersmith.com, and give a real address/fax/tel or whatever, where you can be reached) Why do you put the links in a separate box on which you have to click? Just put them right where you can see them, so everybody knows what you sell. As a start it's definitely not bad, just try to make it bigger and put more stuff in it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||10-21-2001||12:49 PM||||I agree about the email address part, at the very least get an alias pointing to your yahoo account.. same with the phone numbers.<BR>(alias might be info@thefibersmith.com)<P>I've been a web/graphic designer for several years, if there's anything I can help with, just let me know!<P>p.s. who hosts your site?<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||10-21-2001||12:53 PM||||one other thing.. you need to list more prices on the site, and for the kit pages, maybe some build photos, and perhaps maybe an "installation guide" or something like that?<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||10-21-2001||01:24 PM||||I agree with DaRkLoRD. I, too, am a web/graphic designer and design as well as host web sites. I'm sure we could make many suggestions but what I find all too often is, the business doesn't realize how to set up a web site (and the business is responsible for the content) and an inexperienced web designer sometimes doesn't think to ask the right questions. There are improvements which could be made to your site to allow your business to grow and would be very benificial to you but they are far too numerous to elaborate on here.<P>Either DaRkLoRD or myself are available to help but it is best done via email or even phone contact.<P>Feel free to contact me either through my web site  <A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.whgraphics.com</A>  or by phone (toll free) at 866-343-7648.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||10-21-2001||01:30 PM||||I visited the site. I agree with those above. All the links worked for me. The Email change would seem more professional.<BR>Maybe you could have an "Order" page where you can list acceptable payment methods, The contact Email, and maybe even a printable order form and an address to send it to.<BR>Some folks don't like to place orders on-line so this may also increase sales. <BR>Maybe you could do a Zone shipping list like UPS does to give a rough idea what shipping costs would be. Especially the body kits since they would be going out as freight. Graphically it looks good. As another helpful tip, on the items you list as "without lens" or "Lens optional" you could either give a source for the lens or have a separate pic of the lens kits.<P>I would suggest getting together with DaRkLoRD (Steve). <BR>Ooops, or Tgowens, (his post appeared while I was typing)<P>The best part is they know the web hosting AND Fiero's!<BR>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||tomcat06085||10-21-2001||01:43 PM||||I have maintained several corporate websites for established firms and the first rule is make it simple. After you have a tasteful format...preferably, no frames pages...the content has to load quickly. Your site loads quickly, but navigation isn't clear and a yahoo email account isn't a business like way toconduct business. Forms for ordering or a shopping cart account is better. Colors are preferenced by your audience. You need titles and keywords and metatags that the search engines will index to draw the right kind of visitors. Remember, you want to attract visitors that are looking for your products and have the ability to pay.<P>------------------<BR>tomcat<BR>Thanks for the help!||||reg||3
Z||000008||85ZainoGT||10-21-2001||01:59 PM||||you know if you need a website, an awesome website... I got the man to do it... e-mail me if your interested... you cant go wrong here..<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||ferrari_momo||10-21-2001||03:23 PM||||thank you everyone,<BR> i was also hoping that i'd get something like thefibersmith@thefibersmith.com for my email.  that's what i had in mind since the beginning.  as for wheels, i am still having a hard time getting the prices from the vendor.  therefore, i will leave this out of the topic.  but more people are welcome to make comment on my site.  i may not have shopping cart.  but ordering info is a good idea.  i am open to more suggestions.  thank you.<BR>sincerely yours,<BR>pat kalsmith <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dslice||10-21-2001||10:41 PM||||Your Logo is Great. Nice clean site, easy to navigate, loads quick. Need to add product discriptions like wheel sizes and for wheels and genereal kit info.<P>I like it!<P><P>------------------<BR>Rick<P>86GT<BR>84COUP<BR>http://home.mn.rr.com/gmfierogt||||reg||1
Z||000011||BlackDragon||10-21-2001||11:42 PM||||i agree with those above. the site is nice, it looks good, but it could use a little content. you have gotten many suggestions, and you will make your own decisions, but since you are asking, i will give my small suggestions.<BR>i would put the links at the left instead of a scroll thing. it is easier to see, and use. less clicking. <BR>the wheels definitely need some specs, you could make it where you click on the pic of the wheel and it goes to the specs, prices, etc...<BR>definitely needs to have an online ordering method. i myself have almost ordered from you, but i didn't because there was no checkout on your site.<BR>payment options would be a big bonus<BR>there needs to be more contact info, like they said. and also a printable order form. that is almost a must. <BR>thats about all i can think of. in short i agree. its a nice site, but could use a little work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>keep up the good work. im in for a euro rear bumper and lights, just dont have the cash right now. good luck, dont let negative email get you down.<P>------------------<BR>who is General failure? and why is he reading my hard disk?¿?¿?¿<P>big cars may be fast, but i can corner.....<P>BlackDragonsEmail@yahoo.com||||reg||1
Z||000012||Captain Midnight||10-22-2001||12:14 AM||||I can't tell from your site what you do. Do you build cars, build bodies, modify cars? Do your kits come in any other color? What comes in a kit? Are they wired? Can I get differant wheels and tires? Does the kit come with wheels and tires? Do you offer a full kit and a half kit. Can I do part, and you do part? What does this thing cost? Show me the inside. Why don't you have a phone number? Is this a part time job? Do you take VISA? How long before I get it in the mail? How does it attach? Is it garranteed? Show me a picture of what you are selling laying on the ground, so I can see what it looks like, and how many pieces there are. If I wreck it, can you fix it, and how much?||||reg||1
